131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (Over 80% of machine learning algorithms rely on probabilistic models to function effectively. Probability provides the mathematical framework for handling uncertainty inherent in real-world data. When machines make predictions, they must account for incomplete information, noise, and variability. Probabilistic reasoning enables models to quantify confidence levels, weigh evidence appropriately, and make informed decisions even when facing ambiguous situations. This foundation is what allows ML systems to generalize from training data to new, unseen scenarios.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
